  "description": "Thunder Bolt is a climbing course in Cherry Red. Children go up a rope ladder or a climbing wall to a hexagonal net deck, travel along an overhead ring traverse and come down a twin slide. It is meant for confident climbers and gives a group plenty to try in a long, narrow footprint of 28'1\" x 15'1\". Thunder Bolt takes 30 to 35 children. Its listed skills are exploring, confidence building, social skills and critical thinking. It belongs to our NexLev Escapade series and suits schools, parks and resorts with a strip of open ground. Galvanised pipe, roto-moulded parts, composite laminates and play rope have a 3-year warranty. Ask us to mark the safe zone on your drawing.",
